<section class="m-sec">
  <h2>How I work</h2>
  <div class="m-principles">
    <article><h3>Build it, don't just recommend it</h3><p>I'd rather put a working version in front of a team than a slide about one. Most of what this site describes started as a rough first version that teams used, corrected and made their own.</p></article>
    <article><h3>One system of record</h3><p>If the plan lives in threads and decks, it doesn't exist for anyone else. Every redesign I run starts by getting the work into one place people trust.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Put the human where the judgment is</h3><p>Agents can draft most of the work. The design question is which decisions need a person, and making those decisions fast.</p></article>
    <article><h3>Lead without the org chart</h3><p>The biggest changes I've run moved people I didn't manage. That works when the plan is visible, the rehearsal happens before go-live, and readiness is measured, not assumed.</p></article>
  </div>
</section>

